      "id": "2018umman",
      "end": 1599,
      "contributors": [],
      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p><em>Ba\u1e25r-i F\u0101rs</em><span>\u00a0(Persian Gulf):\u00a0It is a sea that emerges from the northern side of the\u00a0</span><em>Ba\u1e25r-i Hind</em><span>\u00a0(Indian Ocean).\u00a0To the east of\u00a0</span><em>Mekr\u0101nt\u012bz</em><span>\u00a0(Makran coast region), at the source of the\u00a0</span><em>Ba\u1e25r-i F\u0101rs</em><span>, it appears visibly like a mouth (</span><em>deh\u0101n</em><span>).\u00a0Likewise, the city of\u00a0</span><em>\u2018Umm\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Oman) is seen on the western side of this sea, and it too is discernible at its mouth, that is, its strait.\u00a0From there it extends, running along the\u00a0</span><em>\u2018Umm\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Oman) coast, and from\u00a0</span><em>\u2018Abb\u0101d\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Abadan, Iran) to\u00a0</span><em>Mehr\u016bb\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Mahru\u0304ba\u0304n, near modern Bushehr).\u00a0Then it passes to\u00a0</span><em>S\u012bn\u012bz</em><span>\u00a0(modern Bushehr/Old Siniz) and stretches southward until it reaches\u00a0</span><em>\u1e2aayy\u0101be</em><span>\u00a0(Khabbah / Khaybah).\u00a0From there it proceeds to\u00a0</span><em>Seyf\u00fc\u2019l-ba\u1e25r</em><span>\u00a0(\u201cthe Sword of the Sea,\u201d Fars coast), and to its east is\u00a0</span><em>S\u012br\u0101f</em><span>\u00a0(Siraf, Iran).\u00a0From that point, it continues along broken mountain ranges and high desert passes and hills, and then, moving further east, it winds around to\u00a0</span><em>\u1e24\u0131\u1e63n Ibn \u2018Amm\u0101re</em><span>\u00a0(Hisn Ibn \u2018Amm\u0101ra) and reaches\u00a0</span><em>H\u00fcrm\u00fcz</em><span>\u00a0(Hormuz), which is the port of\u00a0</span><em>Kirm\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Kerman).\u00a0After that, it stretches toward the southeastern direction, reaching the Makran coast and\u00a0</span><em>\u1e32a\u1e63\u1e63at\u012bz</em><span>.\u00a0[translation]</span></p>",
